invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_point.c
catches: p384_equiv_test
reason: the decoder takes a coordinate at or above p, and the field
  reduces it, so a point has a second encoding. bin/p384_equiv_test
  gives the point whose x is 0 the x of p, under a signature that
  verifies for the point, and wants 0.

--- old
    if (p384_wide_compare(x, p384_wide_modp.m) >= 0 ||
        p384_wide_compare(y, p384_wide_modp.m) >= 0) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    if (p384_wide_compare(y, p384_wide_modp.m) >= 0) {
        return 0;
    }
